[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2893103019","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106556#issuecomment-2893103019","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106556","id":2893103019,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6scT-r","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-20T06:23:31Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T07:49:51Z","body":"Moved here, addressed to @elvisish:\r\n\r\n> Unfortunately it still takes 4 seconds to run the game, it also took around 30 seconds to start Godot :/\r\n\r\nAlso checking the code, all this is switched off when running the editor, it only is active when you are running the game itself. If you are getting slowdowns in the editor, it suggests something else is going on, totally unrelated to this PR.\r\n\r\n* Are you running the most recent artifact?\r\n* Have you run your project or loaded it in 3.6 and confirm it works normally without slowdown?\r\n\r\nThe relevant switch in GLES2 and GLES3 is:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif (!OS::get_singleton()->is_stdout_verbose() && !Engine::get_singleton()->is_editor_hint() && OS::get_singleton()->get_name() == \"Windows\") {\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn both cases it should not be active in the editor (when is_editor_hint() is true).\r\n\r\nAdditionally the correct artifact should print \"Attempting to disable GPU Driver threaded optimization via OpenGL debugging\" when it is active, this is dependent on you having an adapter name with the string \"nvidia\" in it.\r\n\r\nTo clarify, the whole system WILL ONLY BE ACTIVE when verbose output is off.\r\n\r\n_________________________\r\n\r\nI'll see if I can find out what is causing this. To clarify, how long does it take to start with verbose mode?\r\n\r\nIt shouldn't take longer than verbose mode, providing the same debug options are selected (and should take considerably less). It's likely some of the settings I have applied are resulting in more logging, maybe I can test this by emulating it in Linux.\r\n\r\nUPDATE: I've tested in linux and don't get any debug logs in Trucktown, 3D Platformer or TPS demo.\r\nHowever this could be my graphics driver is having no errors etc (Intel iGPU a780).\r\n\r\nAnother possibility is that our debug printing itself is what is causing the difference and maybe flushing std::out or something, in which case the original hypothesis that this is disabling multitheaded optimization might have been incorrect. 🤔\r\n\r\nAlso would you be able to copy into the post some of the verbose logs you get, just to check these are not actually GL errors that are occurring on your GPU. If these are errors then anything could be happening.\r\n\r\nTo clarify let me know (in a post on the PR) whether you are testing on GLES2 or GLES3, that will help.\r\n\r\nAlso an MRP would be useful, does this slowdown occur with an empty project? Can you also test with an empty project?\r\n\r\nAlso if you run the editor from the artifact, then select `help->copy_system_info` from the menu, then paste your system specs here, that might be useful. e.g.:\r\n\r\n`Godot Engine v3.7.dev.custom_build [83474bc39] - X11 - 2 monitors - GLES3 - Mesa Intel(R) Graphics (RPL-S) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700T (24 threads)`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2893103019/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2966235134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106556#issuecomment-2966235134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106556","id":2966235134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wzSf-","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-12T11:21:17Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T11:22:17Z","body":"Ok I've been contacted by @elvisish on X, and I've been able to ascertain some info which helps progress the situation:\r\n\r\n* The PR **does** seem to solve the jitter problem on his windows machine (in the same way as verbose mode)\r\n* The 4 second regression in the editor is unrelated, they are having problems running the artifacts at all (from different PRs)\r\n\r\nSo I think that provides evidence to move this back out of draft and provide as an optional setting for testing in a dev build.\r\n\r\nStill needs a review, but at least testing now confirms that it seems to do the job. :+1: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2966235134/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2966397644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106556#issuecomment-2966397644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106556","id":2966397644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wz6LM","user":{"login":"elvisish","id":16231628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjMxNjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16231628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish","html_url":"https://github.com/elvisish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-12T11:55:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T11:55:29Z","body":"> Ok I've been contacted by @elvisish on X, and I've been able to ascertain some info which helps progress the situation:\r\n> \r\n> * The PR **does** seem to solve the jitter problem on his windows machine (in the same way as verbose mode)\r\n> * The 4 second regression in the editor is unrelated, they are having problems running the artifacts at all (from different PRs)\r\n> \r\n> So I think that provides evidence to move this back out of draft and provide as an optional setting for testing in a dev build.\r\n> \r\n> Still needs a review, but at least testing now confirms that it seems to do the job. 👍\r\n\r\nIt does, and I'll be happy to further test this once there's a non-artifact build that has profiler enabled, currently all artifact builds do not have a functioning profiler, so testing is much more difficult and inaccurate. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2966397644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4062758655","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106556#issuecomment-4062758655","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106556","id":4062758655,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yKMb_","user":{"login":"elvisish","id":16231628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjMxNjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16231628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish","html_url":"https://github.com/elvisish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elvisish/subscriptions","org